Z||000000||Hank is Here||11-07-2000||02:06 PM||||Okay I know it is the nature of a Fiero 2.8 serp belt to squeel, heck mine does it too.  Has anyone done any testing to see which brand belts squeel less or maybe would not squeel at all.   I am going to be putting a Napa (Gates) belt on next and was wondering how that sounds, or better does not sound <P><BR>Mark Johnson ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||11-07-2000||02:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Hank is Here:<BR><B>Okay I know it is the nature of a Fiero 2.8 serp belt to squeel, heck mine does it too.  Has anyone done any testing to see which brand belts squeel less or maybe would not squeel at all.   I am going to be putting a Napa (Gates) belt on next and was wondering how that sounds, or better does not sound <P><BR>Mark Johnson </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I just put it a NAPPA belt today.. Ill let ya know how it go's<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">  <BR>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD"||||reg||6
Z||000002||ThatRickGuy||11-07-2000||02:16 PM||||just out of curiosity, which fieros came w/ the serp belt? I thought it was the L-4s, but I guess I was wrong, my '88 has 2 belts, err, well 1 now that the AC is gone.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||11-07-2000||02:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ThatRickGuy:<BR><B>just out of curiosity, which fieros came w/ the serp belt? I thought it was the L-4s, but I guess I was wrong, my '88 has 2 belts, err, well 1 now that the AC is gone.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>My 87 SE V6 has a serp. belt. with A/C<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">  <BR>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD"||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||11-07-2000||02:55 PM||||The only Fiero's that came with a true serpantine setup were the 87-88 4 cylinders.  The V6's use a serpantine-style wide belt, but don't have a belt-tensioner or anything.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 151,000 miles and counting!         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">      <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||11-07-2000||04:51 PM||||Since I got my GT running, back in May, I have used the following belts (in order):<BR>AutoZone (slipped and frayed)<BR>Advance Auto (Slip and Fray)<BR>Napa (Frayed and broke)<BR>Carquest (been on car for one month)<P>After putting on the carquest belt, I found the culprit... the coolant return that exits the top of the water pump and goes through the chanel under the battery.<P>I would suggest buying the Carquest belt.  They will replace it if anything happens to it.<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||11-07-2000||06:39 PM||||A Serpent belt on any car that's working right will Not squeel. Period. If the belt is squeeling one of three things is wrong.<P>belt tension is off. Belt tensioning device is bad on L4 or belt not adjusted right on V6.<P>PTO device is failing. I.E. Alt, water pump, or AC on an 87-88 L4. Replace the offending part.<P>You got a bad belt or you got crap on the belt. Serpents don't like it if you get oil or coolant on them and then run the car.||||reg||2
